<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE VAULT themed-icon (monochrome) layer, Android 13+.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM ic_launcher_foreground.xml. A launcher
  renders the monochrome layer from its ALPHA CHANNEL ONLY and tints the whole
  thing one wallpaper colour. The coloured foreground paints the slot in the
  background colour and the hairline in the accent, which works when it sits on
  an opaque black tile; flattened to alpha those two rectangles are just more
  ink, so the slot would tint the same colour as the letter and the cut would
  disappear. A themed VAULT icon with no cut is not the mark.

  So here the slot is a HOLE, not a painted bar. android:fillType="evenOdd"
  makes an enclosed subpath subtract from the one containing it.

  WHY THE SLOT IS TWO QUADRILATERALS AND NOT ONE RECTANGLE. A V at cut height is
  two separate diagonal strokes with a gap between them. One rectangle spanning
  both would, under evenOdd, be inside the slot but outside the letter across
  that gap, which counts odd and fills in solid. Each stroke therefore gets its
  own subpath, cut to that stroke's exact width where the slot crosses it, so
  every hole lies wholly inside the letter. The edges are the letter's own:
    left  outer x = 4.4  + (y - 4.5) * 0.37107
    left  inner x = 7.8  + (y - 4.5) * 0.36842
    right inner x = 16.2 - (y - 4.5) * 0.36842
    right outer x = 19.6 - (y - 4.5) * 0.37107
  evaluated at the slot's own top and bottom, y 11.129 and 13.767 in glyph
  units, which is the 11% monogram slot centred on the optical middle of the
  cap height. See ic_launcher_foreground.xml for where those numbers come from.

  The hairline is added back as a filled subpath. Under evenOdd it re-fills
  inside the holes and fills on its own across the gap, so the line reads
  continuously through the letter. That matches the colour icon exactly, where
  the letter and the hairline are both the accent and are indistinguishable.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <group
        android:scaleX="2.895"
        android:scaleY="2.895"
        android:translateX="19.26"
        android:translateY="17.96">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:fillType="evenOdd"
            android:pathData="M4.4,4.5h3.4l4.2,11.4L16.2,4.5h3.4L13.7,20.4h-3.4ZM6.86,11.129L10.242,11.129L11.214,13.767L7.839,13.767ZM13.758,11.129L17.14,11.129L16.161,13.767L12.786,13.767ZM5.617,12.1595L18.383,12.1595L18.383,12.7365L5.617,12.7365Z" />
    </group>
</vector>
